# Build artifacts — zips rebuilt by build.ps1, archived in Nextcloud
E-Tech/releases/*.zip

# Third-party patched mod zips — local bookkeeping only, never published
patched-mods/*.zip

# Superseded third-party zips kept as a local archive. Same reasoning as
# patched-mods/: nothing here is E-Tech's code, nothing here ships with the
# mod, and a public repo has no business redistributing other people's mods
# just because we happened to replace them. absorbed-mods/ is the exception
# and stays tracked — those are the originals of mods whose code was merged
# INTO E-Tech, so they are the licence paper trail.
mods-replaced/*.zip

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp

# Local convenience shortcuts
*.lnk

# Private working docs — session notes, local-machine inventories (stay in
# Nextcloud, never on GitHub)
E-TECH-HANDOFF.md
SESSION-RECAP-*.md
MOD-AUDIT-*.md
CODE-AUDIT-*.md
LOCAL-PATCHED-MODS.md

# Server upload staging folders - big mod zip bundles, distributed via Nextcloud
server-upload-*/

# Local Factorio machine state — this folder is local bookkeeping only, and
# these two change on every launch. The *.zip rule above already covers the
# mods themselves.
patched-mods/mod-settings.dat
patched-mods/mod-list.json
